  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contributing to the Mitigation of Conflict Over Natural Resources Between Farmer and Herder Communities in Adamawa State, Nigeria (COMITAS)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In order to contribute to the mitigation of conflict over natural resources between farmer and herder communities in Adamawa state in Nigeria, IOM, in coordination with Search for Common Ground and Mercy Corps, has designed a comprehensive and integrated approach that seeks to achieve four main outcomes; strengthened traditional conflict resolution, improved trust in authorities, enhanced collaboration in managing the use of natural resources and improved intra- and inter-communal perceptions. IOM builds on its data collection experiences in north-east Nigeria and globally, and its extensive policy engagements with the government of Nigeria, to implement a transhumance tracking tool to strengthen early warning systems of potential conflict triggers and identify solutions early on.</narrative>
  </description>
